    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ownerSegment` field as `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new, in `mapper/`) \u2014 the single source of truth for the derivation, following the existing `Locality`/`Timezone` standalone-class pattern:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevel.of(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when the owner's locality (from `Locality.ofCustomerCode`) is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", \u2026)` expression to call `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSegmentForKnownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) pass, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nNote: the segment reuses `Locality.ofCustomerCode` (the same source the `locality` field uses), so METRO/REGIONAL stays consistent with the owner's reported locality rather than being recomputed from raw city/postcode.",
